# Shared validation (Zod ↔ antdv)

## Source of truth

Contract fields for users / roles / permissions live in **`@vue-nestjs-admin-template/schemas`** (Zod). Nest pipes and Vue forms must not invent parallel min/max/email/uuid rules.

## Layers

1. **Shared Zod** (`packages/schemas`) — API request body contract (`.strict()`, lengths, formats)
2. **API** — `ZodValidationPipe` + thin re-exports under `apps/api/src/**/**.schemas.ts`
3. **Web antdv** — `RuleObject[]` built from shared schemas via `zodRule(...)` in `apps/web/src/validation/`

## Frontend may add more rules

antdv **may** add UX-only rules (required timing, whitespace, confirm-password, async uniqueness messages) **in addition to** shared Zod — never instead of it, and never looser than the shared schema (e.g. do not set `max: 200` if Zod says `max(128)`).

```ts
import { createRoleSchema } from '@vue-nestjs-admin-template/schemas';
import { zodRule } from '@/validation/zod-rule';

name: [
  { required: true, message: 'Name is required' }, // UX OK
  zodRule(createRoleSchema.shape.name),            // contract required
]
```

## Do not

- Duplicate the same constraints only in antdv `rules` without Zod
- Put antdv / Vue imports into `@vue-nestjs-admin-template/schemas` (keep that package Zod-only)
- Drift API-local Zod copies — change `packages/schemas` only
